== en
titulo: I love cooking
intro: Learn how to express strong preferences with encantar, specify who enjoys something, and agree or disagree.
b1.titulo: Preferences: gustar and encantar
b1.texto: "With verbs like **gustar** and **encantar**, the liked thing is the subject and the verb agrees with it:\n\n- Me **gusta** bailar / Me **encanta** cocinar. (activities in infinitive: singular verb)\n- Me **encantan** los libros. (plural noun: plural verb)\n\nTo show who likes something, use indirect object pronouns: **me, te, le, nos, os, les**.\nIf you name the person, precede with **a** and keep the pronoun: **A Pablo le** encanta el fÃºtbol.\n\nTo agree:\n- Positive statement: *Me gusta el cine.* â†’ **A mÃ­ tambiÃ©n.** (disagree: **A mÃ­ no.**)\n- Negative statement: *No me gusta bailar.* â†’ **A mÃ­ tampoco.** (disagree: **A mÃ­ sÃ­.**)"
b2.titulo: Sundays
b3.titulo: Lesson vocabulary
b4.titulo: Structures with gustar and encantar
b4.texto: Notice that infinitives keep the verb in singular, whereas plural nouns require a plural verb.
b5.titulo: Family tastes
b6.titulo: Comprehension question
b6.pregunta: «No me gusta el café». Neither do you. What do you reply?
b6.o0.refuerzo: Exactly! Tampoco is used to agree with a negative statement.
b6.o1.refuerzo: TambiÃ©n is only used after positive statements.
b6.o2.refuerzo: A mÃ­ sÃ­ indicates disagreement (you do like it).
b7.titulo: Complete the sentence
b7.pregunta: Choose the correct form of the verb.
b7.o0.refuerzo: Correct! Infinitives require the singular verb form.
b7.o1.refuerzo: Gustan is used with plural nouns.
b7.o2.refuerzo: Gusto is not the right grammatical form here.
b8.titulo: Order the words
b8.traduccion: My brother loves football.
b9.titulo: Write the translation
b9.pregunta: Translate into Spanish: Â«I love dancing.Â»
p.me encanta.glosa: I love
p.me encanta.consejo: Used for strong liking of an activity or singular item.
p.me encantan.glosa: I love (plural)
p.me encantan.consejo: Plural form agreeing with plural items.
p.le gusta.glosa: he/she likes
p.le gusta.consejo: Used for he, she, or formal you.
p.le encanta.glosa: he/she loves
p.le encanta.consejo: He or she loves something intensely.
p.nos gusta.glosa: we like
p.nos gusta.consejo: Used for we.
p.les gusta.glosa: they like
p.les gusta.consejo: Used for they or plural you.
p.cocinar.glosa: to cook
p.cocinar.consejo: Regular first-conjugation verb.
p.bailar.glosa: to dance
p.bailar.consejo: Regular first-conjugation verb.
